---A filter that you use with the results of a Amazon CloudWatch Internet Monitor query that you created and ran. The query sets up a repository of data that is a subset of your application's Internet Monitor data. FilterParameter is a string that defines how you want to filter the repository of data to return a set of results, based on your criteria.
---@class aws.internetmonitor.FilterParameter
---@field Field? string A data field that you want to filter, to further scope your application's Internet Monitor data in a repository that you created by running a query. A field might be city, for example. The field must be one of the fields that was returned by the specific query that you used to create the repository.
---@field Operator? aws.internetmonitor.Operator The operator to use with the filter field and a value, such as not_equals.
---@field Values? aws.internetmonitor.FilterList One or more values to be used, together with the specified operator, to filter data for a query. For example, you could specify an array of values such as ["Seattle", "Redmond"]. Values in the array are separated by commas.

